  "interpretation": "In HF, candidate improves filtered-reference-to-state tracking vs C5 by about 1.77 mrad while task-to-state changes little. Candidate and C5 have roughly 59–60 mrad task-to-command discrepancy and about 37 mrad command-to-filtered-reference discrepancy. These pairwise gaps are much larger than inner tracking error; this is evidence that the weak task attitude is not explained by inner tracking alone. It does not prove which upstream controller/filter causes the gap."
